<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20931] lnetctl export FILE writes peer configuration to stdout instead of FILE</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20931</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Stumbled upon this while testing something else.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When given a filename, lnetctl export --backup writes the peer section to stdout instead of the requested file. Reproduced on Lustre 2.17.59 over TCP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
sudo lnetctl export --backup /tmp/lnet-before-file.yaml
peer:
-     primary nid: 10.10.0.10@tcp
      Multi-Rail: &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
      peer ni:
      -     nid: 10.10.0.10@tcp
-     primary nid: 10.10.0.21@tcp
      Multi-Rail: &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
      peer ni:
      -     nid: 10.10.0.21@tcp
-     primary nid: 10.10.0.22@tcp
      Multi-Rail: &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
      peer ni:
      -     nid: 10.10.0.22@tcp
-     primary nid: 10.10.0.20@tcp
      Multi-Rail: &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
      peer ni:
      -     nid: 10.10.0.20@tcp

grep -A5 &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;'^peer:'&lt;/span&gt; /tmp/lnet-before-file.yaml

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The grep command returns no output.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test with fix:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
sudo ./lnet/utils/lnetctl export --backup /tmp/lnet-fixed-file.yaml
[root@lustre-client1 lustre-release]# grep -A5 &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;'^peer:'&lt;/span&gt; /tmp/lnet-fixed-file.yaml
peer:
-     primary nid: 10.10.0.10@tcp
      Multi-Rail: &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
      peer ni:
      -     nid: 10.10.0.10@tcp
-     primary nid: 10.10.0.21@tcp 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attached my proposed fix, which passes the selected output stream to yaml_lnet_peer_display() instead of hardcoding stdout.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
